KG42.register("slice-clusters-5fe1dc777995dc9ee18a310b",{"id":"41-data_center_local_markets::v142-d-CL001","paper":"41-data_center_local_markets","title":"Regional scope, buyer-seller roles and scenario permissions for local energy trading","source_pointer":"/clusters/158","node_ids":["COMP-14965fb0e8564001","KG40-e988fed52eadab03","COMP-7f5e3dcddfa1014c","COMP-e80c3b7a1946ecd1","KG40-f19328f0aeb3d626"],"rule_refs":["41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R001","41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R004","41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R005","41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R006","41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R008"],"visible_rule_refs":["41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R001","41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R004","41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R005","41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R006","41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R008"],"suppressed_rule_refs":[],"edges":[],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"interface_annotations":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g01-E04"],"rationale":"The IDC and local market arrangements in the system overview are concretely illustrated in the three-region case. This connection only supplements the case scope and does not infer general exclusive access or a cross-region trading prohibition from it."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E19"],"rationale":"Buyer participation corresponds scenario by scenario to the purchase branch of the trading activity: the proposed framework allows purchasing under power shortage, Case 2 disables local purchasing, and Case 3 retains local purchasing. This is a complementary description of roles and activities and does not add a transaction guarantee."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E19"],"rationale":"The surplus-power supply role is complementary to the sales branch of the trading activity, and facility conditions are retained. Case 2's unsubsidized feedback to the grid and Case 3's local sales prohibition are retained separately and cannot be interchanged as general electricity sales rules."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04"],"rationale":"The trading object corresponds explicitly to shortfall energy purchase and surplus energy sale in the activity; product identification and trading permission are complementary, and they are not judged as duplicate constraints on the basis of shared citations."}],"annotation_policy":"Original D connections are annotations, not additional S edges.","empty_after_chain_suppression":false});
